James inquired about key details of attendees on a departmental visit list, seeking insights into their affiliations, research interests, and potential conversation topics. I planned to gather their current public profiles, specifically targeting pages from the University of Toronto, Rotman, and Max Gluskin House. Initially, I proposed compiling this information via a structured approach but missed delivering a specific JavaScript plan. After James' feedback, I provided a corrected strategy, including an asynchronous function to perform parallel web searches for relevant profiles on each participant, emphasizing a tech-driven method for obtaining concise, practical insights for the visit.
